---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — Crowd';
const description =
  "Crowd is built to forget. It collects as little as possible, keeps it for as short a time as possible, and shares it with no one. Here's exactly what that means.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: June 8, 2026</p>

    <p class="intro">
      Crowd is built to forget. It collects as little as possible, keeps it for
      as short a time as possible, and shares it with no one. This page explains
      exactly what that means.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>Two things, and only while you use the app:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Your location</strong>, when you grant permission. Crowd uses
        your device's foreground location — only while the app is open.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>An anonymous identity token</strong>, generated on your device.
        It's a random value, not tied to your name, email, phone number, or any
        account — because Crowd has no accounts.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <p>
      Your location filters your feed: it shows posts within the reach you choose
      and labels how far away each one is. It is never kept as a history or a
      trail.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your identity token associates the posts and relays you create with your
      device, so the app knows which posts are yours — for as long as those posts
      exist.
    </p>

    <h2>Where it's stored</h2>
    <p>
      Your identity token lives on your device, in iOS Secure Storage. Posts and
      their metadata — text, location, and lifespan — live on Crowd's servers
      only until they expire.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>Everything is temporary by design:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Posts</strong> are deleted automatically when the lifespan you
        set expires.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your identity</strong> rotates — it's replaced with a new one
        once your last active post expires, so your activity can't be linked
        across time.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Crowds</strong> expire after 24 hours. When a crowd ends,
        everything in it is deleted.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>
      No one. Crowd does not sell, rent, or share your data with any third party.
      There are no analytics, no advertising SDKs, and no tracking services
      anywhere in the app.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can clear all of your data at any time from the <strong>You</strong>
      tab. This deletes your posts from our servers and resets your device
      identity. There's nothing to log into and nothing to unsubscribe from.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Crowd is intended for people 17 and older.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about privacy? Email us at
      <a href="mailto:hello@joincrowd.app">hello@joincrowd.app</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 36rem;
  }

  .prose h1 {
    margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.875rem, 5vw, 2.25rem);
  }

  .updated {
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
    color: var(--dust);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  .intro {
    margin: 0 0 2.25rem;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .prose h2 {
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0.625rem;
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
  }

  .prose p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .prose ul {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .prose strong {
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
</style>
